But note: lock action requires origin_node_ready (so we need to activate node before lock). Load action requires origin_availability_node_linked (we have) and candidate_prepared (we will have). Also requires cargo_available (we have). And not origin_availability_locked (so we must load before lock? Wait load requires not locked. If we lock first, load fails. So we must load before lock. But lock gives confirmed and locked. So we need to load before lock to satisfy load's precondition, then lock after load to get confirmed and locked while keeping occupancy (if load does not set locked). However if load does set locked, then after load it's locked, lock precondition fails. So we assume load does not set locked.

Thus order: prepare, activate node, load cargo, lock availability (makes locked and confirmed). This yields: after load: origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked false (assuming load doesn't set locked). After lock: origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, origin_node_occupied stays true (lock does not affect node). Good.

Similarly for destination.

Now we need transport leg assembled and loading authorized etc.

Transport leg assembly requires origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked (precondition). So we need both availabilities locked before assembling leg. Good.

Transport leg loading authorized requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha ? route_task_profile? Actually authorize_transport_leg_loading requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, and not transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we need origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability_alpha.

Thus we need to attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha as well (though goal only requires for destination, but we need for authorization). So we will attach task profile to both.

Now after loading cargo onto origin and destination, we have origin_node_occupied and destination_node_occupied.

Now we need to assemble transport leg. Which assembly action to use? There are several: assemble_transport_leg (requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available). There are also specialized assembly actions for loaded legs: assemble_origin_loaded_leg, assemble_destination_loaded_leg, assemble_fully_loaded_leg. Those have different preconditions regarding node occupied/ready and availability confirmed status.

Goal requires transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_origin_linked, transport_leg_destination_linked, transport_leg_loading_authorized, and also origin_leg_loaded? Not required but maybe needed for loading container etc. Not required.

Goal does not require origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded. So we can use assemble_transport_leg (the basic one) which just assembles leg and links nodes, without setting leg loaded flags.

Thus we will use assemble_transport_leg.

Preconditions: origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available.

We will have all those after we prepare, activate nodes, load cargo, lock availabilities.

Now after assembling leg, we need to authorize loading: authorize_transport_leg_loading requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha, and not transport_leg_loading_authorized.

We have origin_availability_locked (from lock), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (we will attach), transport_leg_assembled (after assemble). So we can authorize.

Now we need to mark origin_availability_dispatch_ready and destination_availability_dispatch_ready.

Mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires: origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha.

Thus after we have lock (locked+confirmed), transport assembled, loading authorized, we can mark origin dispatch ready.

Similarly mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready requires destination_availability_locked, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha.

Thus after we have those, we can mark both.

Now we need to allocate dispatch slot for origin_availability_alpha: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate (origin_availability_alpha), candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate.

We will have dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha after marking, candidate_task_profile_linked (we attached), dispatch_slot_available initially? Currently dispatch_slot_alpha is not available because it's linked to shift_candidate_alpha. But after we dispatch shift_candidate_alpha (execute_schedule_dispatch), the slot will become available. So we need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha first to free slot, then allocate to origin_availability_alpha, then dispatch origin_availability_alpha.

But note: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate also requires candidate_task_profile_linked for the candidate (origin_availability_alpha). We'll have that.

Now after allocating, we need to dispatch origin_availability_alpha via execute_origin_dispatch (requires dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha, candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot, not dispatched origin_availability_alpha). We have vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha (init). So candidate_vehicle_linked exists. Good.

After dispatch, we get vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and dispatch_slot_available.

Now we also need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha. We can do that before allocating slot to origin, or after? If we dispatch shift_candidate_alpha first, slot becomes available, we allocate to origin, then dispatch origin, slot becomes available again. Goal requires dispatch_slot_available at end, which will be true after origin dispatch.

Now we also need dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (goal). So we need to execute execute_schedule_dispatch for shift_candidate_alpha.

Now we also need compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha. Initially it's linked to shift_candidate_alpha. We need to release it via release_compliance_certificate action (requires candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha). After releasing, compliance_certificate_available becomes true.

Thus we need to release compliance certificate from shift_candidate_alpha.

Now we also need to ensure that after releasing, we still have shift_candidate_alpha dispatched? The release action does not affect dispatched. So fine.

Now we need to ensure we have vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma after dispatching shift_candidate_alpha. The execute_schedule_dispatch for shift_candidate_alpha will make vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (since candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma). Good.

Now we need to ensure we have vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha after dispatching origin_availability_alpha.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_prepared for origin and destination. We'll do attach_task_profile and confirm_candidate_preparedness.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_task_profile_linked for destination_availability_alpha (goal). We'll attach.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability_alpha (for authorization). We'll attach.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_origin_availability_linked shift_candidate_alpha? Not needed for goal but may be needed for some actions? Not.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_destination_availability_linked shift_candidate_alpha? Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha (already). Good.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta (already). Good.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma (already). Good.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_alpha transport_leg_alpha (already). Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_alpha loading_container_alpha (already). Not needed for goal but maybe for loading container onto leg? Not required.

Now we need to ensure we have loading_container_available etc. Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have equipment_available etc. Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have service_window_available etc. Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have skill_certificate_available etc. Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have operational_constraint_available etc. Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha? Already true in init. Goal does not require it; but it's okay if remains true.

Now we need to ensure we have dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha? Initially true. After we execute execute_schedule_dispatch, dispatch_allocated will become false? Let's check effect of execute_schedule_dispatch: (dispatched ?candidate) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). It does NOT affect dispatch_allocated. So dispatch_allocated remains true after dispatch? Actually the action does not modify dispatch_allocated. So dispatch_allocated stays true. However goal does not require dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha; it's okay if remains true.

But we need dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha (goal). We'll allocate via allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate, which sets dispatch_allocated true.

Now we need to ensure dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha after marking.

Now we need to ensure dispatch_ready shift_candidate_alpha? Not required but okay.

Now we need to ensure dispatched origin_availability_alpha and dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (goal). We'll achieve via execute_origin_dispatch and execute_schedule_dispatch.

Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared for origin and destination.

Now we need to ensure candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (we will attach).

Now we need to ensure compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha (we will release from shift_candidate_alpha).

Now we need to ensure origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready via activate actions.

Now we need to ensure origin_node_occupied and destination_node_occupied via load actions.

Now we need to ensure transport_leg_assembled etc.

Now we need to ensure transport_leg_loading_authorized via authorize.

Now we need to ensure origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed via lock actions.

Now we need to ensure origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked via lock actions.

Now we need to ensure candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha via allocate.

Now we need to ensure dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha via allocate.

Now we need to ensure dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha via mark actions.

Now we need to ensure dispatched origin_availability_alpha via execute_origin_dispatch.

Now we need to ensure dispatched shift_candidate_alpha via execute_schedule_dispatch.

Now we need to ensure vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and vehicle_unit_gamma via dispatch actions.

Now we need to ensure dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha at end (after origin dispatch).

Now we need to ensure that we don't inadvertently cause any conflicts: